[2.582, "o", "Read uv.lock. Running openllmetry. The first run builds an environment per library, which takes about a minute.\r\n"]
[4.082, "o", "Read uv.lock. Checking: openllmetry.\r\n"]
[4.262, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.442, "o", "OpenLLMetry  (anthropic 2.4.0, openai 3.42.1, opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http 1.45.2, opentelemetry-instrumentation-anthropic 0.62.4, opentelemetry-instrumentation-openai 0.62.4, opentelemetry-sdk 1.45.2)\r\n"]
[4.622, "o", "  ST01 Ghost span: 5 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[4.802, "o", "    The app made the call, and no finished span ever reaches a backend.\r\n"]
[4.982, "o", "    Cost figure for one call: -100%, at list price\r\n"]
[5.162, "o", "    For example, anthropic/stream-early-exit: never ended: anthropic.chat\r\n"]
[5.342, "o", "    Tracked at https://github.com/traceloop/openllmetry/issues/4536\r\n"]
[5.522, "o", "    Tracked at https://github.com/traceloop/openllmetry/issues/4643\r\n"]
[5.702, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST01\r\n"]
[5.882, "o", "  ST02 Double span: 14 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[6.062, "o", "    One call reports its token usage on two spans.\r\n"]
[6.242, "o", "    Cost figure for one call: +100% in a backend that sums across spans, at list price\r\n"]
[6.422, "o", "    For example, anthropic/basic: expected 1, reported 2: usage on 2 spans: anthropic.messages.create, anthropic.chat\r\n"]
[6.602, "o", "    Today: Let one side report the call: set ANTHROPIC_OPEN_TELEMETRY=false, or pass open_telemetry=False to the client.\r\n"]
[6.782, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST02\r\n"]
[9.962, "o", "  ST03 Cache-blind tokens: 2 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[10.142, "o", "    Cached tokens are left out of the input count, or their own counts are wrong.\r\n"]
[10.322, "o", "    Cost figure for one call: -10.8%, at list price\r\n"]
[10.502, "o", "    For example, openai/cache-write: expected 3181, reported nothing\r\n"]
[10.682, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST03\r\n"]
[10.862, "o", "  ST04 Phantom tokens: 7 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[11.042, "o", "    The span reports more tokens than the provider sent, or invents a count.\r\n"]
[11.222, "o", "    Cost figure for one call: +0.2%, at list price\r\n"]
[11.402, "o", "    For example, anthropic/stream: expected 419, reported 420\r\n"]
[11.582, "o", "    Tracked at https://github.com/traceloop/openllmetry/pull/4377\r\n"]
[11.762, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST04\r\n"]
[11.942, "o", "  ST05 Vanishing tokens: 2 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[12.122, "o", "    The span reports fewer tokens than the provider sent, or none.\r\n"]
[12.302, "o", "    Cost figure for one call: -100%, at list price\r\n"]
[12.482, "o", "    For example, openai/stream-helper: expected 2137, reported nothing\r\n"]
[12.662, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST05\r\n"]
[12.842, "o", "  ST06 Hidden reasoning: 1 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[13.022, "o", "    The reasoning tokens that the provider reported do not appear on the span.\r\n"]
[13.202, "o", "    For example, openai/stream-reasoning: expected 1931, reported nothing\r\n"]
[13.382, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST06\r\n"]
[13.562, "o", "  ST07 False OK: 2 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[13.742, "o", "    A call failed, and its span does not say so, or does not say how.\r\n"]
[13.922, "o", "    For example, openai/stream-dropped: expected ERROR, reported OK\r\n"]
[14.102, "o", "    Tracked at https://github.com/traceloop/openllmetry/pull/4535\r\n"]
[14.282, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST07\r\n"]
[14.462, "o", "  ST09 Silent stop: 2 of 45 scenarios\r\n"]
[14.642, "o", "    The finish reason is missing or wrong.\r\n"]
[14.822, "o", "    For example, openai/stream-helper: expected stop, reported nothing\r\n"]
[15.002, "o", "    More: https://plexito-de.github.io/spantruth/bugs.html#ST09\r\n"]
[15.182, "o", "  Other failing checks: response_id, response_model\r\n"]
[15.362, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.542, "o", "This checks your library versions against a local fake provider. It does not run your application, so it cannot see settings in your code, such as open_telemetry=False, and it knows nothing about your backend.\r\n"]
